                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6d292865-0cd8-30ff-91bd-35ddd9561af6",
                        "entry_id": "03fce726-ed28-3ad5-b1b9-359f23bfd806",
                        "glosses": [
                            "уменьш. к пёстрый"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "70f8cdff-0d53-42d8-bb40-8f92742dbd79",
                                "sense_id": "6d292865-0cd8-30ff-91bd-35ddd9561af6",
                                "text": "Перед зеркалом стояли две малышки и разговаривали. Одна была в синем платье из блестящей шёлковой материи, с таким же шёлковым пояском, завязанным сзади бантом. У неё были голубые глаза и тёмные волосы, заплетённые в длинную косу. Другая была в пёстреньком платье с розовыми и фиолетовыми цветочками. Волосы у неё были светлые, почти белые, спускавшиеся на плечи волнами."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "db4c51c8-2f0c-48c0-9693-8a6427f16228",
                        "source_entry_id": "03fce726-ed28-3ad5-b1b9-359f23bfd806",
                        "source_sense_id": "6d292865-0cd8-30ff-91bd-35ddd9561af6",
                        "target_lang_word": "motley",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "motley",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "37e7f3f6-624f-3254-a5f9-8815f4a9a080",
                                        "entry_id": "56b316f5-dde3-3eec-bb2d-124416c22ebf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Comprising greatly varied elements, to the point of incongruity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9bb2c99-bcb3-4610-a76e-465358d63812",
                                                "sense_id": "37e7f3f6-624f-3254-a5f9-8815f4a9a080",
                                                "text": "I met a fool i' th' forest, / A motley' fool."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb461849-ed23-40ca-b07e-08a1bf71815b",
                                                "sense_id": "37e7f3f6-624f-3254-a5f9-8815f4a9a080",
                                                "text": "Carried somehow, somewhither, for some reason, on these surging floods, were these travelers,[…]. Even such a boat as the Mount Vernon offered a total deck space so cramped as to leave secrecy or privacy well out of the question, even had the motley and democratic assemblage of passengers been disposed to accord either."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85c218aa-2b90-4af8-a908-e9f516ecb12d",
                                                "sense_id": "37e7f3f6-624f-3254-a5f9-8815f4a9a080",
                                                "text": "\"One of them can see you, and one of them can see an empty hallway.\" Reynders narrowed her bleary eyes — she wasn't wearing her glasses, for some reason — as though momentarily uncertain which sight she was seeing. She apparently decided in favour of their motley group. \"I'm the one who can see you. The one who can see you can talk to you. The one who can't talk to you can see you too, sometimes, but she doesn't want to because she knows you're not there. Where she is.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8825e929-0172-3194-8529-20b278f2592c",
                                        "entry_id": "56b316f5-dde3-3eec-bb2d-124416c22ebf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having many colours; variegated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "motley",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "681873b1-2efa-336d-8abd-4ab9e2913443",
                                        "entry_id": "279c54d9-dfa1-3319-8bb2-60d26e454dc9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An incongruous mixture."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4578d872-b3d3-312c-9383-90927136bf63",
                                        "entry_id": "279c54d9-dfa1-3319-8bb2-60d26e454dc9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A jester's multicoloured clothes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cbd67960-467b-3dcd-8276-1485135a8bfd",
                                        "entry_id": "279c54d9-dfa1-3319-8bb2-60d26e454dc9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A jester; a fool."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "050be5c0-9794-4263-ad4c-3a7bf443eafc",
                                                "sense_id": "cbd67960-467b-3dcd-8276-1485135a8bfd",
                                                "text": "Wil you be married, Motley?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f83a0582-c941-486e-b428-8a6118230e9d",
                                                "sense_id": "cbd67960-467b-3dcd-8276-1485135a8bfd",
                                                "text": "Alas, 'tis true, I have gone here and there, / And made myself a motley to the view, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ebc938f9-583d-4c3d-b83b-45539fcc62b3",
                        "source_entry_id": "03fce726-ed28-3ad5-b1b9-359f23bfd806",
                        "source_sense_id": "6d292865-0cd8-30ff-91bd-35ddd9561af6",
                        "target_lang_word": "gaudy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gaudy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c8bf584e-65a0-36e6-8a56-0a802c84de51",
                                        "entry_id": "5f5ebc70-6e66-324d-9567-3a6f5aaca162",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Very showy or ornamented, now especially when excessive, or in a tasteless or vulgar manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a2f1cf3-4226-4fb1-bd51-b5e710f1ace4",
                                                "sense_id": "c8bf584e-65a0-36e6-8a56-0a802c84de51",
                                                "text": "Costly thy habit as thy purse can buy, / But not expressed in fancy; rich, not gaudy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29675c42-cfef-48ae-b4cc-20c5050409b2",
                                                "sense_id": "c8bf584e-65a0-36e6-8a56-0a802c84de51",
                                                "text": "Though, I confeſs, Paris has its Charms; but to me they are like thoſe of a Coquette, gay and gavvdy; they ſerve to amuſe vvith, but a Man vvould not chuſe to be marry'd to them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0421ea4d-5293-4516-bc0b-6eb3f623c6f5",
                                                "sense_id": "c8bf584e-65a0-36e6-8a56-0a802c84de51",
                                                "text": "The rooms were lofty and handsome, and their furniture suitable to the fortune of its proprietor; but Elizabeth saw, with admiration of his taste, that it was neither gaudy nor uselessly fine; with less of splendour, and more real elegance, than the furniture of Rosings."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10dc7796-3382-48f7-a7bc-9a4e4237ad4d",
                                                "sense_id": "c8bf584e-65a0-36e6-8a56-0a802c84de51",
                                                "text": "A faded, and an ancient dragon he was; and many a wintry storm of rain, snow, sleet, and hail, had changed his colour from a gaudy blue to a faint lack-lustre shade of gray."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ecdd1f2-5f96-4786-9c03-d2cccb8a3e22",
                                                "sense_id": "c8bf584e-65a0-36e6-8a56-0a802c84de51",
                                                "text": "A large gaudy, flowing cravat, and an ill-used silk hat, set well back on the wearer's head, completed this somewhat noticeable costume."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18a857bd-0190-465f-bd67-3339d1bccb7a",
                                                "sense_id": "c8bf584e-65a0-36e6-8a56-0a802c84de51",
                                                "text": "Gaudy jewellery might offend some people's sense of style. But former heavyweight champion and grilling-machine entrepreneur George Foreman is philosophical about today's craze for bling-bling."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "574199f1-a53f-3a13-ba1a-71d979c5cd98",
                                        "entry_id": "5f5ebc70-6e66-324d-9567-3a6f5aaca162",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fun; merry; festive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9da7c3cd-0479-4a01-b630-dc3873498857",
                                                "sense_id": "574199f1-a53f-3a13-ba1a-71d979c5cd98",
                                                "text": "Let's have one other gaudy night."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20ace9f1-ae84-4d1e-a889-be1cf07407c9",
                                                "sense_id": "574199f1-a53f-3a13-ba1a-71d979c5cd98",
                                                "text": "And for my strange petition I will make\nAmends hereafter by some gaudy day"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b843c99b-57c7-4f58-b170-8402e76854e0",
                                                "sense_id": "574199f1-a53f-3a13-ba1a-71d979c5cd98",
                                                "text": "And then, there he was, slim and handsome, and dressed the gaudiest and prettiest you ever saw..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "gaudy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4030893e-597a-369c-871e-1fd9ac31b28d",
                                        "entry_id": "39979445-127a-3340-95c0-686b39590462",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One of the large beads in the rosary at which the paternoster is recited."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9430895-1957-4a92-8d3e-fdb6c83a33f8",
                                                "sense_id": "4030893e-597a-369c-871e-1fd9ac31b28d",
                                                "text": "In 1458, the owner of the precious book, which had been taken from the martyr’s body at the block, left a rosary of 50 coral beads with gold gaudies, to his “beloved, most blessed Saint Richard Scrope,” to help in his canonization, with a prayer to God that it might be granted of His great grace."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "157ba132-b583-4859-8ec5-b507d2b81350",
                                                "sense_id": "4030893e-597a-369c-871e-1fd9ac31b28d",
                                                "text": "The circling year was to him like the rosary over which he recited his aves and paternosters; the “gaudies” or larger beads were the holidays set at regular intervals along the string, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a02bd2c-420b-4ae7-8d24-3ef9f48343b8",
                                                "sense_id": "4030893e-597a-369c-871e-1fd9ac31b28d",
                                                "text": "She wore a coral trinket on her arms, / A set of beads, the gaudies tricked in green, / Whence hung a golden brooch of brightest sheen […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "gaudy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "51f56994-c870-3d50-b13a-aa16188ab1ee",
                                        "entry_id": "f4060efe-c394-3487-9dba-2d232b75cbca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A reunion held by one of the colleges of the University of Oxford for alumni, normally during the long vacation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
